 "note": "Echostage: a big-room rig arranged in a crown pattern. 20 par7 across five zones — a sweeping 8-lamp upstage arc that peaks at centre and drops at the wings, 4 side-pillar pars on diagonal mounts giving the room its width, 4 front-wash pars on a V-truss (outer high, centre low), and 4 floor uplights on the deck — plus 4 head13 moving heads in a diamond (an outer pair crowning the arc and an inner pair centred below it). Par count is a multiple of four so groupsOf splits cleanly. The layout has real depth: upstage at y=0, sides at y=1..2, front truss at y=3.8, so travelling effects cross the room. Positions in metres in the AUDIENCE frame: at = [x, depth, height], +x = audience's right, depth grows toward audience, height from floor.",
